Preface:

E!-Logfile Viewer (also called E!-LfV in this doc) is as long freely 
Distributable as long as the Archive Contents stay intact! At least 
these files should be in the Archive:

E!-LfV ................ Main-Program ............... 11924 Bytes
E!-LfV.c .............. Source Code ................  2714 Bytes
E!-LfV.doc ............ This documentation .........  3274 Bytes

Full Archive Size: 10185 Bytes


Installation:

First Copy E!-LfV into your DOORS:, if you haven't assigned it, you
should know yourself where to find it. 

Then edit the EX.BBSMenus File. Add the following line to the 'Global
Commands' Part of that file:

610, LfV, 0, "32", "\#4Doors:E!-LfV <full path and your 'callers' Logfile>\"

Save the File, and select the Master Window's Pull-Down-Menu
Extras/Re-Load/Menus. Thats all for the Installation..

Now make a Sysop-Login to your BBS, and type LfV at the main Menu. If 
everything is installed correctly you should see something like that:


   ------- E!-LogFile Viewer 1.0 (C)opyright 2/95 by ACP-Development -------

      Amiga Crackpoint --- * --- +43 2252 46519 --- * --- USR V.34 & ISDN
          FaaastLane BBS -- * -- +43 1 8761678 -- * -- v32.bis  14400

   #    Handle                          Date
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1.)  Mike Hammer                     <Mon 23-Jan-1995 4:34pm>
   2.)  Mike                            <Mon 23-Jan-1995 7:35pm>
   3.)  Mike Hammer                     <Mon 23-Jan-1995 7:59pm>
   4.)  Mike                            <Mon 23-Jan-1995 7:56pm>
   5.)  Mike                            <Mon 23-Jan-1995 9:04pm>
   6.)  Spiderman                       <Mon 23-Jan-1995 11:01pm>
   7.)  Mike Hammer                     <Mon 23-Jan-1995 11:06pm>
   8.)  Spiderman                       <Mon 23-Jan-1995 11:12pm>
   9.)  SouL SuCKeR                     <Wed 25-Jan-1995 10:01pm>
  10.)  Picard                          <Wed 25-Jan-1995 10:49pm>

Please enter # to View (Q to quit):

Enter now the number of the caller you wish to get displayed detailed, 
and E!-LfV will display the matching part of your 'Callers'.

Attention: E!-LfV will *ONLY* work, when you left the Logfile Structure in
the Language file unchanged! Maybe future versions of E!-LfV will be
configurable for custom Logfile configurations...  

Further your 'Callers' File shouldn't be larger than 30K, otherwise the
list generated by E!-LfV gets very large. We suggest you to use
ACP-Strip1.0 (available on the Aminet or in any mailbox near you) in the
TEXT.LOGOUT file of E!, so your logfile keeps constantly the same size, for 
expample 30K. 

